pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% A coefficient above i64::MAX, so the whole `pol` derivation below sits one
% width tier above the proved kernel's NARROW coefficient domain. Its purpose is
% to pin, in tests/kernel_verify_expected.txt, that --kernel-verify covers that
% tier: the narrow replay stands down on width, the bridge re-runs the same step
% at the kernel's unbounded (BigInt) instantiation, and the run reports "nothing
% outside the proved fragment" with a fully composed shadow database. Before the
% kernel was made generic over its coefficient domain this instance pinned the
% opposite -- a counted `constraint-not-i64-representable` skip -- and that hole
% is where two of the three red-team wrong verdicts hid; see the development design notes
% section 7.3. Do not "simplify" the coefficient: the instance is worthless
% below 2^63.
f 2;
pol 2 2 +;
output NONE;
conclusion NONE;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
